from h34 import *
M=mcq;F=tf;S=short;N=num
chapter(3,'evs','plants-and-animals-live-together','Plants and Animals Live Together',
 ('Look around a plant','Wherever there are plants, there are animals too: on the leaves, in the branches, under the roots and in the soil. Elephants feed on grass, a caterpillar chews a leaf, earthworms live in the soil, a tailorbird sings on a tree and ants build a nest from leaves. This chapter shows how plants give animals food, shelter and a place to rest, and what soil is made of.'),
 [('Animals live on and around plants',['Many animals live on, around and under plants. A moth rests on a leaf, a woodpecker lives on a tree trunk, a frog rests on a leaf and a butterfly sits on a flower.','Squirrels and a barbet use tree hollows to hide, rest and nest. Ants build their nest with leaves, and earthworms live in the soil.','Animals choose to live near plants because plants give them food, shelter and a safe place.']),
  ('How animals use plants',['Camels eat the leaves of plants, and monkeys love the fruits of plants. Caterpillars munch on leaves for food.','Sunbirds and butterflies drink nectar, the sweet juice of flowers.','Owls and other birds use hollows in trees to raise their young. Squirrels and crows use twigs to build their nests.','Tailorbirds stitch leaves together to build nests. Bats and leopards rest on tree branches and find shelter there.','So plants give animals food, shelter and resting places, and animals depend on plants.']),
  ('Life in the soil',['Soil is the topmost layer of the Earth\'s surface. It is made from rocks that have broken into tiny pieces, and from old leaves, roots, stems and living and dead animals such as insects.','We can feel soil with our hands. It can be dry, damp, rough, smooth, hard or grainy. After rain it feels and smells different from dry soil.','Soil has many small creatures. On the top we find ants, termites, small beetles and grasshoppers. When it rains, earthworms and millipedes may come out.','Some insects wait in the soil for the rains to come. Seeds may stay in the soil for a long time and sprout when it rains or when they are watered, which is why new plants and animals appear in the monsoon.','Soil far from plants looks different from soil near a plant, because there are fewer leaves and roots in it.']),
  ('Listening to birds',['We can close our eyes and listen to birds. Cupping our ears with our hands and facing the direction of the sound helps us to hear it more clearly.','Different birds make different sounds, and a pigeon\'s sound is like gutru gu.','We hear more bird sounds early in the morning and in the evening, when birds are most active. If we hear few birds, there may not be many trees or there may be a lot of noise.'])],
 [('Name three ways animals use plants.',[('Some animals eat leaves, fruits, nectar or seeds.','Plants are food.'),('Some use trees for nests, such as owls in hollows and tailorbirds with stitched leaves.','Plants are shelter.'),('Some rest on branches, such as bats and leopards.','Plants give a place to rest.')]),
  ('What is soil made of?',[('Rocks broken into tiny pieces.','Rocks wear away slowly.'),('Old leaves, roots and stems.','Plant parts that have died.'),('Living and dead animals such as insects.','Small creatures live and die in soil.')])],
 ('Tell how plants help animals and how animals live on plants.',['Food such as leaves, fruit and nectar','Shelter like hollows and nests','Resting places like branches','Soil full of small creatures'],['Animals do not need plants','Soil is only sand']),
 ['Plants give animals food, shelter and resting places.','Soil is made of tiny rock pieces, old plant parts and animals.','Many small creatures live in soil, and more come out after rain.','Different birds make different sounds.','Seeds can stay in soil and sprout when it rains.'],
 [M('1',1,'What do sunbirds and butterflies drink?','Nectar from flowers',[('Water from soil','They drink nectar'),('Milk','They drink nectar')],'Nectar is the sweet juice of flowers.'),
  M('2',1,'Which animal uses a tree hollow to raise its young?','Owl',[('Camel','A camel eats leaves'),('Elephant','An elephant eats grass')],'Owls use hollows in trees.'),
  M('3',1,'What does a tailorbird use to build its nest?','Stitched leaves',[('Mud only','Tailorbirds stitch leaves'),('Stones','They use leaves')],'Tailorbirds stitch leaves.'),
  M('4',1,'What is soil?','The top layer of the Earth\'s surface',[('A kind of animal','Soil is not living'),('Only sand','It has many parts')],'Soil is made of tiny rock pieces and plant and animal remains.'),
  M('5',2,'Which animal eats leaves of plants?','Caterpillar',[('Bat','A bat rests on branches'),('Leopard','A leopard rests on branches')],'Caterpillars munch leaves.'),
  M('6',2,'Which animals may come out of the soil after rain?','Earthworms and millipedes',[('Lions','Lions do not live in soil'),('Camels','Camels live elsewhere')],'They come up when the soil is wet.'),
  F('7',2,'Seeds can stay in soil for a long time and sprout when it rains.',True,'They need water to grow.'),
  M('8',2,'Which animal rests on tree branches?','Bat',[('Earthworm','It lives in soil'),('Camel','It lives on land')],'Bats and leopards rest on branches.'),
  F('9',2,'Soil near a plant and soil far from plants is always the same.',False,'Soil near plants has leaves and roots in it.'),
  S('10',2,'What is the sweet juice of flowers called?',['nectar','Nectar'],'Butterflies and sunbirds drink it.'),
  M('11',3,'When do we hear most bird sounds?','Early morning and evening',[('At midnight only','Birds are not so active then'),('Never','We can hear birds'),],'Birds are most active at these times.'),
  M('12',3,'Why do animals live near plants?','Plants give food and shelter',[('Plants are noisy','Not a reason'),('Plants are bright','Not a reason')],'Plants give food, shelter and rest.')],
 keep=['soil','nectar','shelter'])
